# Simulation output — 3.9G, ~46k files on disk. This rule keeps NEW output out of
# `git status`. It does NOT untrack the 31 files here that are ALREADY in the index
# (the docs, the analysis scripts, and the whole formal_reap/ Lean project including
# PROOF_LEDGER.md) — .gitignore has no effect on tracked paths. The old comment said
# "never tracked", which was false and would mislead anyone adding a new proof module:
# a new file under this path is invisible to `git status` and easy to lose. Ignored so
# it stays out of
# `git status` noise and cannot be swept in by an accidental `git add`.
09_TOOLS/03_SIMULATIONS/

# Generated dimension routes are deterministically rendered by
# 12_PUBLIC_SITE/render_dimension_site.py and intentionally tracked. They are
# declared current, directly deployed static pages; a checkout or deployment
# artifact must contain the exact reviewed bytes without relying on an implicit
# host-side generator step.
